1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,600
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:05,840
and for entertainment purposes only.
Viewer discretion is advised.

3
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,640
Are you okay?

4
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,280
I'm not.

5
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:23,400
Nakun.

6
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:26,320
Don't force him.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,640
-But…
-But what?

8
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,400
-ARE YOU HERE? OR ANOTHER TIME?
- I'M HERE

9
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:39,600
<i>Should I be sent there,</i>
<i>then I shall drag you down with me!</i>

10
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:05,800
Klao.

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,320
If death is to claim you,

12
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,880
it shall be by my hand alone, Phop!

13
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,120
Let go!

14
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,160
Phop!

15
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:56,040
Klao!

16
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,320
My Lord.

17
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,120
-Klao.
-My Lord.

18
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,800
We must go the physician at once.

19
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:01,720
No!

20
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,000
-My Lord.
-No!

21
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,040
I must get to Klao!

22
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,400
Let go of me!

23
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:17,080
Klao.

24
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:23,200
Klao!

25
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,960
The wounds have healed.

26
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:44,880
But what concerns me is that
he has grown terribly frail.

27
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,880
I fear a sickness may take hold.

28
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,640
Do take some nourishment, Phop.

29
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,200
I spent the day
preparing these treats for you.

30
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:03,600
Phop.

31
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,160
My dear.

32
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:12,960
Phop!

33
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,880
Phop.

34
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:15,840
Dear.

35
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,680
-Phop.
-Phop.

36
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:22,120
Rest now, and take the remedies
as the physician prescribed, I beg.

37
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,720
I cannot, Mother.

38
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,760
I must find Klao.

39
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:37,960
Phop.

40
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,720
Rest easy now.

41
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:46,200
I have dispatched the patrol
to search for him.

42
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,360
But a week has already passed, Father.

43
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,000
Why then has no one yet found him?

44
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:04,360
Illness may already have
taken hold of him.

45
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,120
No one knows what fate has befallen him…

46
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,080
how frightened he may be…

47
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:19,120
or how troubled his heart is.

48
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,800
Son.

49
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:32,680
Phop.

50
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:34,680
Phop.

51
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,000
-Phop…
-Phop.

52
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,760
Sickness may claim you, Phop.

53
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,520
Chuay.

54
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,880
Let us return to our quarters.

55
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,280
Staying up will not bring
Master Klao back.

56
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,680
No.

57
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,520
If he is to return…

58
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,280
and I am not here for him,

59
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,640
who then will tend to his needs?

60
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,760
He has taken no nourishment,

61
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,560
not even water.

62
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,680
He is still lost in his delusions,

63
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:02,360
writing letters to Master Klao
as he always does.

64
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:05,360
We must endure a little longer.

65
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:09,320
Tend well to our lord's heart
and to our own.

66
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:14,000
The skies that follow a storm
are ever magnificent.

67
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,200
<i>"My dearest,</i>

68
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,880
<i>the father and son have at last confessed.</i>

69
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:46,960
<i>The evidence was the opium shipment list</i>
<i>concealed beneath their manor,</i>

70
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,000
<i>together with your father's letter,</i>

71
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:51,800
<i>wherein he declined and threatened</i>
<i>High Lord Horathibodi,</i>

72
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:54,640
<i>declaring he would denounce</i>
<i>the High Lord at court.</i>

73
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,600
<i>I have been granted the rank of Viscount</i>

74
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,840
<i>for capturing those</i>
<i>who defrauded the land.</i>

75
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:04,640
<i>Yet this triumph</i>

76
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:07,160
<i>means nothing,</i>

77
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:10,640
<i>for it is empty without you</i>
<i>to share in its joy.</i>

78
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,160
<i>Where are you, I wonder?</i>

79
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,600
<i>Do you still remember me?</i>

80
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:26,040
<i>And do you long for me as I long for you?</i>

81
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:29,040
<i>Return to me</i>

82
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,320
<i>and be my happiness once more, Klao.</i>

83
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,880
<i>Viscount Phop."</i>

84
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:51,960
VISCOUNT PHOP

85
00:07:55,680 --> 00:08:00,480
YOURS MOST DEARLY, PHOP

86
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:13,560
THEE: HE LEFT

87
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,280
<i>I have not yet given up.</i>

88
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,120
<i>I shall find my way to my dearest Klao,</i>

89
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:25,040
<i>as I have promised.</i>

90
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,560
Your drink.

91
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,240
Thank you.

92
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,480
No wonder

93
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:51,320
you kept asking Nakun to stay.

94
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,440
It was so that
he could talk to the hotel owner.

95
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:57,400
Technically, he's not the owner.

96
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,920
He's helping his uncle out.

97
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:03,080
So this friend of yours doesn't have a job

98
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:05,560
and is about to get evicted too.

99
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:10,280
How about asking him
to work at the cafe

100
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,880
while he looks for another job?

101
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:14,360
Whoa.

102
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,600
You're such a generous soul.

103
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,360
Still, you're not as handsome as I am.

104
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:21,280
Thee, come here.

105
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,800
He's helping us out, all right?

106
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:31,560
Thank you kindly.

107
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:52,400
Are you okay with this, Nakun?

108
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,760
-Whoa.
-Gorgeous, isn't it?

109
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,880
-What do you think?
-It's massive.

110
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:58,640
Let me help you.

111
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,240
<i>People say life gets turned upside down</i>

112
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,240
<i>when you turn 25, right?</i>

113
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,800
<i>I'm in my early 20s,</i>

114
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,680
<i>yet in just a few weeks,</i>

115
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,600
<i>my life has changed a lot.</i>

116
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,680
Let's head inside.

117
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:43,080
<i>And in this new life</i>
<i>I'm trying to get used to,</i>

118
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:47,040
<i>I've met familiar faces from my past life.</i>

119
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,480
<i>It's not about seeking attention from men.</i>

120
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:59,760
<i>As women,</i>
<i>we take care of ourselves for ourselves.</i>

121
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,480
<i>Varna, my fragrance brand,</i>

122
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,240
<i>is made for women</i>

123
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:06,520
<i>who live for themselves</i>
<i>and conquer each day with confidence.</i>

124
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:09,920
<i>If you're interested,</i>
<i>type the number one in the chat.</i>

125
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,200
<i>The order are coming in. And--</i>

126
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,240
Yes, boss.

127
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,080
Here you go.

128
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,720
Da Hong Pao Frappuccino
with tapioca pearls.

129
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,440
And…

130
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:32,000
Matcha with no sugar.

131
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,320
Excellent work.

132
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,400
Took you awhile.

133
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,160
I'm thirsty.

134
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,080
It's here.

135
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,040
Here are your drinks.

136
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:01,680
Whoa.

137
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,080
They look delicious.

138
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,200
Yours looks really good.

139
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,440
This one's your favorite, right?

140
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:15,120
You're just rambling.
I'm going to talk to Nakun.

141
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,240
How disappointing.

142
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,480
Right now?

143
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,560
Five minutes.

144
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,280
Oh, come on.

145
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,440
Watch where you're going.

146
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:30,960
Stay calm, Thee.

147
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:33,680
Mind your words.

148
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:36,040
You were the one who bumped into him.

149
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,680
I'm really sorry.

150
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,000
I didn't mean it.

151
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,320
I'm really in a hurry.

152
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,240
Are you hurt?

153
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:53,240
Did you get hurt?

154
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,800
No, not a big deal.

155
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:58,960
Oh, it's okay.

156
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,560
Let me clean it up.

157
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:08,840
<i>Everyone gets a chance</i>
<i>to start anew in this life.</i>

158
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:12,520
<i>Whether we cross paths again</i>
<i>is another question.</i>

159
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:15,000
<i>And if we do, what will be the next step?</i>

160
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,160
A-Chai, it's okay.
I'll mop the floor myself.

161
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,680
Make him another drink.

162
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:20,760
No, no.

163
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,200
It's okay.

164
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,240
I'm in a hurry.

165
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,360
So sorry, guys.

166
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,200
"A-Chai"?

167
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:29,440
He called you "A-Chai"?

168
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:30,720
No, boss.

169
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:31,840
My name is Achi.

170
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,400
-Of course.
-Who did he mean?

171
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:34,760
I get it.

172
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:39,160
Who? Who is A-Chai?

173
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,400
I didn't say A-Chai, boss.

174
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:43,440
I said, A-yes!

175
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:45,080
-Yes!
-You said A-Chai.

176
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,520
No, I said, yes!

177
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,000
-Like this.
-You said A-Chai.

178
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:48,960
I said yes!

179
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,400
What's wrong with me?
I can't stop working!

180
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,680
-Like this.
-Whose name?

181
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,560
-It's Achi.
-Don't be afraid, Achi.

182
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:56,400
Don't be, sweetie.

183
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,640
-Yes.
-Your name is not A-Chai, it's Achi.

184
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,000
Understood?

185
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:00,920
Yes, I do.

186
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,160
You've got this.

187
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,480
It's Achi.

188
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:14,840
FARMER PHOP

189
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,040
K-DRAMA PHOP

190
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,680
I wonder what kind of new life
Phop is living.

191
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,040
Phop.

192
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,840
I still haven't given up on you.

193
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,080
But I think I'll stop being sad now

194
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,880
so that, if I happen to run into you,

195
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,560
all you'll see is my smile.

196
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,480
How does that sound?

197
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:54,120
<i>In Buddhism, a bond from a past life</i>

198
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,200
<i>is not simply about a couple promising</i>

199
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:00,720
<i>to love each other across lifetimes,</i>
<i>as it is often portrayed in dramas.</i>

200
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,720
<i>It means that every relationship</i>

201
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,240
<i>and action from the past</i>

202
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,839
<i>helps shape the present.</i>

203
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:12,480
<i>We meet in this life</i>
<i>because of shared karma.</i>

204
00:17:13,119 --> 00:17:15,119
<i>That is why our paths cross in this life.</i>

205
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,599
Earlier this evening,

206
00:17:24,319 --> 00:17:25,640
you were really cool, Thee.

207
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:30,160
I thought you were about to fight him.

208
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,840
But you kept your cool.

209
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:37,960
If there had been a fight,
you might have really gotten hurt.

210
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,080
I care about you.

211
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,120
Forget it.

212
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,160
You'll think I'm flirting again.

213
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:49,280
Let's listen the podcast.

214
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:53,800
You once asked me
about multiple lifetimes.

215
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:56,000
<i>We studied time travel literature today.</i>

216
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,160
The topic was about multiple lifetimes.

217
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:00,960
Do you believe in stuff like that?

218
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:04,080
Perhaps our paths crossed in past lives.

219
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,120
Then I don't believe in it.

220
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,960
This lifetime is more than enough.

221
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,680
Can I ask you the same question?

222
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:19,360
You might not believe this…

223
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:22,960
but I once dreamed…

224
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,880
I was a doctor.

225
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,560
Nakun asked me to buy some plasters,

226
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:32,240
but I bought plaster mix instead.

227
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,720
There's no way I'd ever be a doctor.

228
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,320
Thee.

229
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:45,920
I also had a dream.

230
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:51,760
Can you stay and talk with me at my place?

231
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,240
Since my birthday,

232
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,840
these are the only things
I've been dreaming about.

233
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,520
You're telling me

234
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,120
you remember your past life?

235
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,640
I don't think so.

236
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:27,360
Maybe it's because I've been into
those hit period dramas lately.

237
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,680
But…

238
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:34,640
I've been having the same dreams
almost every night.

239
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,440
In my dreams…

240
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:44,080
it feels like I once fell for you, Thee.

241
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,000
And I really cared about you.

242
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,880
But you

243
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:50,120
kept rejecting me.

244
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:55,120
When I woke up,
all I could do was cry.

245
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,880
Don't say I'm out of my mind,

246
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:03,160
but these dreams felt so real.

247
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,640
They made me realize…

248
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,560
I've been really mean to you.

249
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:25,080
I ditched you countless times.

250
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,840
No, Pun.

251
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:33,760
Don't cry.

252
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,840
I never get mad at you, you know?

253
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:41,520
I know I joke around a lot,

254
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,520
so it's not surprising
that you'd ditch me.

255
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,720
But

256
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,520
every time I tell you I love you,

257
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:53,680
it's never a joke.

258
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:52,080
Wait.

259
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:54,640
I confessed first,

260
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,840
so I make the first move, right?

261
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,120
You're joking around again, Thee.

262
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:07,560
Well then,

263
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:10,600
that didn't count.

264
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,880
You want to make the first move?

265
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:17,920
Come here then.

266
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:48,840
You're okay, right?

267
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:52,680
This isn't too fast, is it?

268
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:01,760
It was already too late, Thee.

269
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:26,880
Don't close your eyes.

270
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:29,760
I've been working out just for this.

271
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:06,520
I'm not sure

272
00:29:07,320 --> 00:29:09,680
if this is a little too late…

273
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:15,720
but I love you too, Thee.

274
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:35,600
Nakun.

275
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:37,920
Are you doing the emoji challenge or what?

276
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:41,040
I just…

277
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:43,440
You…

278
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:45,560
Why did Pun say yes?

279
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,880
Oh, by the way, congrats, guys.

280
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:57,480
<i>Kaew, your wish has finally come true.</i>

281
00:30:57,560 --> 00:30:59,840
<i>You can love each other openly now, Jom.</i>

282
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,720
Relax, Nakun. I can't breathe.

283
00:31:11,080 --> 00:31:12,640
How can I relax?

284
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:14,760
Well,

285
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:16,920
Thee's been trying
to win your heart for ages.

286
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:19,520
Nakun, you've been single for ages.

287
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:20,880
Have someone in mind?

288
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:22,800
When will it be your turn?

289
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:26,280
My turn? Nonsense.

290
00:31:26,360 --> 00:31:27,960
I don't like anyone.

291
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:33,960
<i>My heart is waiting for Phop.</i>

292
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:44,120
Madam!

293
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,920
-Hey.
-Olive! Somebody, help!

294
00:31:48,720 --> 00:31:49,600
Grab her, please!

295
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:50,760
-Darling.
-Grab her!

296
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:16,160
PHOP 8070 BANGKOK

297
00:32:32,280 --> 00:32:33,440
You!

298
00:32:33,520 --> 00:32:34,680
Are you all right?

299
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:43,200
Whoa.

300
00:32:59,480 --> 00:33:00,320
It's fine.

301
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:24,320
He's my relative.
My uncle's son.

302
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:28,720
He just graduated from law school,
and is now a barrister.

303
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:30,360
He's helping out at the hotel here.

304
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:32,600
He's extremely diligent and kind.

305
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:36,520
Phop is actually the person
who got this job for you.

306
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,200
Can't take your eyes off him, can you?

307
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,680
How about becoming my brother-in-law
instead of my friend?

308
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:49,000
Gosh.

309
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:55,160
Thee,

310
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,720
take me to the toilet, will you?

311
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:10,080
Apologies on behalf of my driver.

312
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:15,159
The driver couldn't see the little girl.

313
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,239
No problem at all.

314
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:21,840
I'm fine, and so is the girl.

315
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:27,360
But when you called me,

316
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,320
I thought you already knew me.

317
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:32,880
No.

318
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:35,520
I was calling "you" as a pronoun.

319
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:40,800
I just found out your name is Nakun.

320
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:44,600
Have you known Thee long?

321
00:34:47,239 --> 00:34:49,600
Well, since I was a freshman.

322
00:34:51,639 --> 00:34:53,800
But he never mentioned

323
00:34:54,600 --> 00:34:56,560
a relative this kind-hearted.

324
00:34:56,639 --> 00:34:59,880
Thank you for letting me work here.

325
00:35:03,040 --> 00:35:05,960
He's also never mentioned
he had a friend this sweet.

326
00:35:10,640 --> 00:35:12,320
But now that we've met…

327
00:35:15,600 --> 00:35:17,240
it's a pleasure to meet you.

328
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,160
<i>It has to be Phop.</i>

329
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:33,120
<i>He looks just like him,</i>

330
00:35:34,120 --> 00:35:36,120
<i>but he doesn't seem to remember me.</i>

331
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:45,920
That's quite the handshake.

332
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,200
An itchy palm for luck, huh?

333
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:51,000
Oh, Nakun.

334
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:53,720
You're taking Introduction to Law, right?

335
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:55,720
You want him to help you with the finals?

336
00:35:57,760 --> 00:35:59,800
He says he can't wrap his head around it.

337
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:03,000
Did he really say that?

338
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:07,240
Uh, yeah.

339
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:11,840
I mean, I actually have
a great memory.

340
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:12,760
But

341
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:16,120
when it comes to law,

342
00:36:16,760 --> 00:36:18,080
it might not be my cup of tea.

343
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:35,320
Can I have your contact details?

344
00:36:48,240 --> 00:36:49,080
I'm Phop.

345
00:36:53,520 --> 00:36:57,440
<i>If he can't remember me,</i>
<i>I'll make sure he does.</i>

346
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:02,520
PHOP

347
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:05,440
<i>Is it too bold to text him first?</i>

348
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:21,080
ARE YOU FREE TO HELP ME
STUDY LAW TOMORROW?

349
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:23,240
<i>Study law?</i>

350
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:25,000
<i>Sounds too stressful.</i>

351
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:28,120
<i>Would we have a moment</i>
<i>to reminisce about our past?</i>

352
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:33,480
ARE YOU ASLEEP YET?

353
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:35,840
<i>Whoa.</i>

354
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:37,320
<i>He texted me first?</i>

355
00:37:39,520 --> 00:37:41,560
<i>If I reply not yet,</i>

356
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:45,160
<i>is it too much of a giveaway</i>
<i>that I've been waiting for him?</i>

357
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:49,280
<i>Or if I say I'm already sleeping,</i>
<i>will we keep talking?</i>

358
00:37:54,520 --> 00:37:56,280
JUST FINISHED WORK
GOING TO SLEEP SOON

359
00:38:00,040 --> 00:38:03,680
DON'T STAY UP TOO LATE
YOU'LL GET SICK

360
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:08,920
<i>You're as warm as a clay stove.</i>

361
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:12,040
<i>Wait, no.</i>

362
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:14,120
<i>This is the modern era.</i>

363
00:38:14,200 --> 00:38:15,720
<i>So he's more like a microwave.</i>

364
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:22,680
WILL DO

365
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:23,920
LOL

366
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:25,000
SLEEPING AT THE CAFE?

367
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:28,120
SAFE TRIP, GOOD NIGHT AND NO DREAMS

368
00:38:42,600 --> 00:38:44,360
Good night, and sweet dreams.

369
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:49,640
No, no dreams.

370
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:54,680
It will let us sleep soundly
and get a good rest.

371
00:38:57,600 --> 00:39:00,960
SAFE TRIP, GOOD NIGHT AND NO DREAMS

372
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:10,040
DON'T FORGET YOUR THAI HISTORY
ASSIGNMENT OR YOU'LL FAIL

373
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:21,960
PHOP

374
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:24,440
I FAILED THAI HISTORY

375
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:26,360
I NEED TO SUBMIT A REPORT FOR EXTRA CREDIT

376
00:39:26,440 --> 00:39:28,280
ARE YOU AVAILABLE THIS WEEKEND?

377
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:30,000
CAN YOU TAKE ME BACK TO AYUTTHAYA?

378
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:49,400
Does my voice sound that bad?

379
00:40:52,320 --> 00:40:53,320
It sounds great.

380
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:55,520
The song is meaningful too.

381
00:41:18,760 --> 00:41:21,200
There's something I wanted to ask
since we left the city.

382
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:25,560
Why did you say,
"Take me back to Ayutthaya,"

383
00:41:26,520 --> 00:41:28,640
and not, "Take me to Ayutthaya"?

384
00:41:45,080 --> 00:41:46,360
So…

385
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:49,520
My mom lives here.

386
00:42:10,600 --> 00:42:13,440
PA MAN KITCHEN JUNGLE AND FISH DISHES

387
00:42:30,080 --> 00:42:31,120
Need a boost, Phop?

388
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:41,640
Sheesh.

389
00:42:41,720 --> 00:42:43,560
Are you trying to give him
an indirect kiss?

390
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:45,640
Thee.

391
00:42:45,720 --> 00:42:47,600
Don't tease Nakun and Phop like that.

392
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:48,680
Look at him.

393
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:50,000
Nakun is blushing already.

394
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,320
I'm not.

395
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:53,240
It's hot out here.

396
00:42:59,280 --> 00:43:01,960
The perfect balance
of sweet and sour, Ichitan.

397
00:43:04,920 --> 00:43:06,360
What would you like to order?

398
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:11,200
Today's special is
spicy red curry with wallago.

399
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:13,520
We've got some remarkably large ones.

400
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:21,080
Ma'am.

401
00:43:21,160 --> 00:43:23,280
Do you serve spicy ant-larvae salad here?

402
00:43:23,360 --> 00:43:24,640
We don't, unfortunately.

403
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:26,400
It's not the right season for it.

404
00:43:28,280 --> 00:43:30,960
Well then,
please take a look at the menu.

405
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:33,960
Let me know
when you're ready to order, okay?

406
00:43:57,280 --> 00:43:58,640
The temple is stunning.

407
00:43:58,720 --> 00:44:00,000
Wow.

408
00:44:05,720 --> 00:44:07,600
<i>It is of the finest quality,</i>

409
00:44:08,480 --> 00:44:10,520
brought by traders from across China.

410
00:44:10,600 --> 00:44:11,760
Thanks.

411
00:44:44,080 --> 00:44:45,600
Guys!

412
00:45:23,800 --> 00:45:25,080
Ever been here before?

413
00:45:25,160 --> 00:45:26,280
Familiar, actually.

414
00:45:26,360 --> 00:45:28,600
This is absolutely gorgeous!

415
00:45:35,240 --> 00:45:36,080
So beautiful.

416
00:45:36,160 --> 00:45:37,080
-Whoa.
-Agreed.

417
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:39,760
Let's take group selfies, guys.

418
00:45:41,920 --> 00:45:42,920
Come on.

419
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:44,640
-Right here?
-Yeah.

420
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:53,000
A bit closer, guys.

421
00:46:05,120 --> 00:46:06,480
A kiss is fine for family.

422
00:46:06,560 --> 00:46:07,760
Kiss on the cheek!

423
00:46:11,440 --> 00:46:12,720
A bit closer.

424
00:46:12,800 --> 00:46:14,720
-A bit closer.
-Yeah!

425
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:30,880
Three, two, one.

426
00:46:34,560 --> 00:46:36,680
I'm gonna tell your mom you're dating.

427
00:46:36,760 --> 00:46:37,840
You!

428
00:46:38,880 --> 00:46:39,800
Stop it already.

429
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:40,880
Stop what?

430
00:46:48,200 --> 00:46:50,040
What's the matter, Nakun?

431
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:51,280
Tired?

432
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:52,800
Oh, I just…

433
00:46:53,480 --> 00:46:55,360
This is really taking me back.

434
00:47:23,360 --> 00:47:25,400
Thee has been complaining about the heat,

435
00:47:25,480 --> 00:47:28,360
so I told Pun to take him to a cafe.

436
00:47:31,280 --> 00:47:32,880
Should we get changed and head back?

437
00:47:36,680 --> 00:47:38,640
Can we stay like this for a bit longer?

438
00:47:39,960 --> 00:47:42,240
Seeing you in that outfit,

439
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:45,040
it's like you've stepped out of the past.

440
00:47:46,400 --> 00:47:48,200
Strolling around here

441
00:47:48,720 --> 00:47:51,400
feels like
we've been transported back to that era.

442
00:47:54,920 --> 00:47:56,560
Let's go to the top of the prang.

443
00:47:57,480 --> 00:47:59,880
Its condition remains
as pristine as it was back then.

444
00:48:14,920 --> 00:48:15,880
Phop.

445
00:48:17,440 --> 00:48:18,760
You study law, don't you?

446
00:48:21,080 --> 00:48:24,040
How do you know
the prang's condition

447
00:48:25,000 --> 00:48:26,200
is still the same?

448
00:48:30,600 --> 00:48:31,440
You…

449
00:48:33,560 --> 00:48:35,640
You remember me, don't you?

450
00:49:52,120 --> 00:49:54,480
You must have been
extremely shocked back then, right?

451
00:49:54,560 --> 00:49:56,000
I'm sorry…

452
00:49:58,480 --> 00:50:00,320
I left you all alone.

453
00:50:00,400 --> 00:50:02,440
I tried to find my way back to you,

454
00:50:02,520 --> 00:50:03,720
but…

455
00:50:03,800 --> 00:50:05,160
It's okay.

456
00:50:06,160 --> 00:50:07,640
You weren't to blame at all.

457
00:50:09,160 --> 00:50:11,560
Time travel isn't something
that can be done easily.

458
00:50:15,600 --> 00:50:17,360
Don't blame yourself. It's okay.

459
00:50:20,760 --> 00:50:23,800
I searched everywhere for you,

460
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:27,960
but I couldn't find any traces of you.

461
00:50:33,640 --> 00:50:35,440
But we're together at last, aren't we?

462
00:50:36,720 --> 00:50:38,680
And we'll never be apart again.

463
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:00,240
But, Phop…

464
00:51:01,720 --> 00:51:04,040
do you remember everything
since the beginning?

465
00:51:04,920 --> 00:51:06,040
No.

466
00:51:07,760 --> 00:51:10,040
Everything came back to me…

467
00:51:13,960 --> 00:51:15,840
when I turned 20

468
00:51:16,560 --> 00:51:17,760
last year.

469
00:51:29,280 --> 00:51:30,680
MOM: HAPPY BIRTHDAY

470
00:51:30,760 --> 00:51:32,040
JUJU: HBD

471
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:33,920
MAY: HAPPY BIRTHDAY

472
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:35,320
NAM: HBD

473
00:51:37,040 --> 00:51:38,320
<i>That was a kiss?</i>

474
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:39,360
<i>Let me show you.</i>

475
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:40,720
<i>You keep saying this and that.</i>

476
00:51:40,800 --> 00:51:42,600
<i>Things aren't the same anymore.</i>

477
00:51:42,680 --> 00:51:43,720
<i>I am more than pleased.</i>

478
00:51:43,800 --> 00:51:45,240
<i>My concern is not unrequited.</i>

479
00:51:45,320 --> 00:51:46,800
I spoke in Phichit,

480
00:51:46,880 --> 00:51:48,320
<i>I told you I'm not Klao!</i>

481
00:51:48,400 --> 00:51:49,480
Stop calling me that!

482
00:51:49,560 --> 00:51:51,000
<i>I shall seek you out</i>

483
00:51:51,840 --> 00:51:53,360
<i>until I find you</i>

484
00:51:53,440 --> 00:51:54,600
<i>and love you once more.</i>

485
00:51:58,880 --> 00:52:01,600
<i>The memories suddenly rushed into my head,</i>

486
00:52:01,680 --> 00:52:03,200
<i>as if</i>

487
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:06,600
<i>my past life was connected to this one.</i>

488
00:52:06,680 --> 00:52:08,240
<i>I then started to miss Klao,</i>

489
00:52:08,320 --> 00:52:10,920
<i>who came back after disappearing.</i>

490
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:14,440
I'm Nahathai's son,

491
00:52:15,680 --> 00:52:18,080
the deputy from the nearby mango orchard.

492
00:52:18,160 --> 00:52:20,360
<i>Then I remembered what Harn had said.</i>

493
00:52:20,440 --> 00:52:21,480
<i>At last,</i>

494
00:52:21,560 --> 00:52:23,680
Klao had once again been slain,

495
00:52:24,280 --> 00:52:27,240
despite my having already killed him
with my own hands.

496
00:52:31,360 --> 00:52:33,400
<i>That was when I came up with a theory.</i>

497
00:52:33,480 --> 00:52:34,840
<i>A wild one too.</i>

498
00:52:36,400 --> 00:52:37,760
PHATTANATADA
ACADEMIC AWARDS 2023

499
00:52:41,560 --> 00:52:43,720
NAKUN PHATTANATADA

500
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:46,640
<i>Klao didn't lose his memories.</i>

501
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:51,280
<i>Instead…</i>

502
00:52:51,360 --> 00:52:52,800
He's from present time.

503
00:52:53,760 --> 00:52:54,760
Whoa.

504
00:52:54,840 --> 00:52:55,800
Phop.

505
00:52:57,560 --> 00:52:59,280
What's next?

506
00:53:00,480 --> 00:53:02,760
Did you keep looking for me after that?

507
00:53:05,360 --> 00:53:08,320
Then I found out that
you study at the same university as Thee.

508
00:53:08,400 --> 00:53:10,480
Everything is on the Internet.

509
00:53:10,560 --> 00:53:13,000
So I went to see Thee at the university.

510
00:53:16,440 --> 00:53:17,800
Nakun's contact.

511
00:53:17,880 --> 00:53:19,040
Here's Nakun's contact.

512
00:53:19,120 --> 00:53:20,320
-His contact!
-Stop!

513
00:53:20,400 --> 00:53:21,440
Stop. Don't do this.

514
00:53:21,520 --> 00:53:22,480
Can you guys see this?

515
00:53:22,560 --> 00:53:23,920
-Give it!
-Nakun's!

516
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:25,200
This is Nakun's contact!

517
00:53:25,280 --> 00:53:26,800
You can't do this!

518
00:53:26,880 --> 00:53:28,160
You'll need to find someone.

519
00:53:28,240 --> 00:53:29,840
I don't want to!

520
00:53:29,920 --> 00:53:32,000
Nakun's contact!

521
00:53:32,080 --> 00:53:33,360
<i>Just seeing you there</i>

522
00:53:33,960 --> 00:53:35,960
<i>already made me want to go and hug you.</i>

523
00:53:36,560 --> 00:53:40,040
<i>But then I thought,</i>
<i>you probably didn't know anything yet.</i>

524
00:53:40,120 --> 00:53:41,160
His contact!

525
00:53:41,240 --> 00:53:43,480
<i>You probably</i>
<i>hadn't traveled back in time yet.</i>

526
00:53:44,320 --> 00:53:45,560
Here's Nakun's contact.

527
00:53:45,640 --> 00:53:47,200
It's his contact, Nakun's contact.

528
00:53:48,680 --> 00:53:50,280
Nakun's contact!

529
00:53:52,280 --> 00:53:54,080
<i>If you had found me first,</i>

530
00:53:54,840 --> 00:53:56,640
<i>everything might have changed.</i>

531
00:53:58,160 --> 00:53:59,840
<i>So all I could do was wait,</i>

532
00:54:00,520 --> 00:54:03,120
<i>just like I did in my past life.</i>

533
00:54:03,200 --> 00:54:04,200
<i>Gosh, how unfortunate.</i>

534
00:54:10,120 --> 00:54:11,960
I called you to help me with my work.

535
00:54:12,040 --> 00:54:13,240
What are you laughing at?

536
00:54:13,320 --> 00:54:15,040
Look at Nakun, my buddy.

537
00:54:15,760 --> 00:54:17,920
He celebrated his birthday last night.

538
00:54:18,000 --> 00:54:20,680
They say bad things happen
when you turn 25, right?

539
00:54:20,760 --> 00:54:21,880
But he's only 20.

540
00:54:22,440 --> 00:54:24,240
Yet he's been bombarded with misfortunes.

541
00:54:26,160 --> 00:54:28,240
<i>That was when I came up with a theory.</i>

542
00:54:28,320 --> 00:54:31,440
<i>If Harn killed Klao</i>
<i>and made him disappear at the age of 20,</i>

543
00:54:32,320 --> 00:54:35,520
<i>would that bring you back to Ayutthaya</i>
<i>when you turned 20?</i>

544
00:54:35,600 --> 00:54:37,920
Do you want to help ease his misfortunes?

545
00:54:41,680 --> 00:54:42,880
<i>That's why…</i>

546
00:54:44,320 --> 00:54:45,520
<i>I came up with a plan.</i>

547
00:54:45,600 --> 00:54:47,480
Your mom knows a certain fortune teller.

548
00:54:50,200 --> 00:54:51,320
Listen.

549
00:54:51,400 --> 00:54:52,840
I refuse to take part in anything

550
00:54:52,920 --> 00:54:55,400
that compromises the ethics
of the prophetic craft.

551
00:54:59,960 --> 00:55:02,280
I simply want you to listen to me,
fortune teller.

552
00:55:03,360 --> 00:55:06,160
It's up to you
whether you believe me or not.

553
00:55:07,600 --> 00:55:09,080
It was 400 years ago.

554
00:55:09,600 --> 00:55:12,360
You were on the very cusp
of becoming the oracle of the court.

555
00:55:13,040 --> 00:55:14,280
But you were cast out,

556
00:55:15,480 --> 00:55:18,840
as you were condemned
for being effeminate.

557
00:55:21,640 --> 00:55:23,760
Are you here to steal my job?

558
00:55:23,840 --> 00:55:26,600
Thus, you ended up as a wandering oracle,

559
00:55:26,680 --> 00:55:28,840
lending aid to others
in whatever ways you could.

560
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:32,680
This shard of a shooting star

561
00:55:33,400 --> 00:55:35,840
is something you gave to someone.

562
00:55:37,640 --> 00:55:38,680
Does it look familiar?

563
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:48,160
This isn't fake.

564
00:55:48,240 --> 00:55:50,680
It's called a wishing stone.

565
00:56:05,080 --> 00:56:06,520
You probably know

566
00:56:07,080 --> 00:56:08,920
what it can do, don't you?

567
00:56:09,560 --> 00:56:11,520
With strong will and determination,

568
00:56:12,600 --> 00:56:15,240
any wish will come true.

569
00:56:16,200 --> 00:56:17,800
Precisely.

570
00:56:17,880 --> 00:56:19,600
It will be yours…

571
00:56:22,000 --> 00:56:23,640
if you help me.

572
00:56:29,160 --> 00:56:33,120
<i>I asked the fortune teller</i>
<i>to advise you to return to Ayutthaya,</i>

573
00:56:33,200 --> 00:56:35,840
<i>as it might send you back to the past</i>
<i>and reunite us.</i>

574
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:37,560
Hey! Nakun!

575
00:56:37,640 --> 00:56:38,480
Nakun!

576
00:56:38,560 --> 00:56:40,280
-Klao!
-Are you okay, Nakun?

577
00:56:42,320 --> 00:56:44,880
<i>Since then,</i>
<i>I've been keeping an eye on you,</i>

578
00:56:45,440 --> 00:56:47,560
<i>making sure you're safe.</i>

579
00:56:53,320 --> 00:56:56,320
<i>And I was actually brought back</i>
<i>to that time period.</i>

580
00:56:57,400 --> 00:56:59,440
Time doesn't move in a straight line.

581
00:57:00,680 --> 00:57:02,680
It moves in cycles,

582
00:57:03,400 --> 00:57:04,600
doesn't it?

583
00:57:09,840 --> 00:57:13,280
Why didn't you say anything
when we were at the hotel?

584
00:57:14,360 --> 00:57:16,200
Even though everything fell into place,

585
00:57:17,040 --> 00:57:18,800
it was only a theory.

586
00:57:19,880 --> 00:57:22,200
There was a chance
that you wouldn't recognize me.

587
00:57:29,720 --> 00:57:31,080
Likewise.

588
00:57:31,160 --> 00:57:34,560
I actually wanted to hug you
when we met in front of the hotel.

589
00:57:34,640 --> 00:57:36,920
If you couldn't recognize me

590
00:57:37,600 --> 00:57:38,720
in this lifetime,

591
00:57:38,800 --> 00:57:41,480
people might think
not only have I lost my wits,

592
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:46,400
but they might even
put me behind bars.

593
00:57:53,080 --> 00:57:54,040
At first,

594
00:57:54,640 --> 00:57:56,560
I thought it was all just a dream.

595
00:57:57,960 --> 00:57:59,280
If it weren't

596
00:57:59,360 --> 00:58:02,480
for the clothes I was wearing
when I traveled through time,

597
00:58:02,560 --> 00:58:04,480
I might have thought I'd lost my mind.

598
00:58:06,880 --> 00:58:08,000
Still…

599
00:58:10,880 --> 00:58:12,480
I'm glad

600
00:58:12,560 --> 00:58:13,920
that

601
00:58:14,000 --> 00:58:16,640
we were finally
able to find one another once more.

602
00:58:25,160 --> 00:58:28,040
From now on,
I'll never let you slip away again.

603
00:58:31,760 --> 00:58:34,200
You're going to get tired
of seeing me every day.

604
00:58:40,360 --> 00:58:41,760
If this wasn't a sacred place…

605
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:48,880
Then let's go somewhere else.

606
00:58:48,960 --> 00:58:52,160
What did you have in mind?

607
00:59:00,640 --> 00:59:02,720
I was thinking of taking you
to this event.

608
00:59:03,600 --> 00:59:05,320
It's being held at a nearby university.

609
00:59:07,800 --> 00:59:10,200
UNSOLVED MYSTERIES FROM AYUTTHAYA:
A NOBLEMAN'S BETRAYAL

610
00:59:10,280 --> 00:59:11,520
CORRUPTION IN THE OPIUM TRADE

611
00:59:20,240 --> 00:59:22,120
CORRUPTION IN THE OPIUM TRADE
RECORDS MISSING

612
01:00:49,680 --> 01:00:52,920
We discovered this document

613
01:00:53,000 --> 01:00:57,200
buried in an area that was believed to be

614
01:00:57,280 --> 01:00:59,920
the estate of a certain high lord.

615
01:01:00,960 --> 01:01:03,440
In the surrounding area,

616
01:01:03,520 --> 01:01:05,000
there are also Wat Sema Muang

617
01:01:05,080 --> 01:01:08,080
and the canal market
mentioned in the document.

618
01:01:08,160 --> 01:01:10,920
It is probably equivalent

619
01:01:11,840 --> 01:01:13,200
to the ancient Chinese market

620
01:01:13,280 --> 01:01:17,160
by Khlong Takhian,

621
01:01:17,240 --> 01:01:19,120
as it was a vast market

622
01:01:19,200 --> 01:01:21,960
accessible by both boat and land,

623
01:01:22,040 --> 01:01:24,600
consisting of brothels

624
01:01:24,680 --> 01:01:27,800
and countless Chinese establishments.

625
01:01:31,840 --> 01:01:33,560
-Thank you very much.
-Thank you.

626
01:01:39,920 --> 01:01:41,400
It's very close to my mom's place.

627
01:01:43,360 --> 01:01:45,160
What you did in the past

628
01:01:46,120 --> 01:01:48,240
really changed the present.

629
01:01:53,240 --> 01:01:56,280
Do you think
you'll meet Lord Preechaphibal?

630
01:01:59,640 --> 01:02:01,000
Maybe not.

631
01:02:03,840 --> 01:02:04,920
Or…

632
01:02:06,240 --> 01:02:07,600
Maybe I already met him.

633
01:02:09,840 --> 01:02:10,720
Phop.

634
01:02:11,520 --> 01:02:13,720
Can you take me to my mom's place?

635
01:02:44,480 --> 01:02:45,520
This day,

636
01:02:46,360 --> 01:02:48,400
I owe you my deepest gratitude.

637
01:02:52,280 --> 01:02:54,400
It brings me joy
to see you in such delight.

638
01:02:54,920 --> 01:02:56,240
Rest now.

639
01:02:56,320 --> 01:02:58,000
I shall come fetch you tomorrow.

640
01:03:03,360 --> 01:03:07,000
Would you like a drink
or some snacks first?

641
01:03:09,040 --> 01:03:10,240
Is your mother home?

642
01:03:11,040 --> 01:03:12,600
I don't want to bother her.

643
01:03:12,680 --> 01:03:15,080
Nakun, you're home?

644
01:03:23,840 --> 01:03:24,880
Hello, Mother.

645
01:03:35,800 --> 01:03:36,840
Hello.

646
01:03:36,920 --> 01:03:38,320
Come inside, will you?

647
01:03:38,400 --> 01:03:41,000
I just finished preparing mangoes
with sweet fish sauce dip.

648
01:03:53,720 --> 01:03:55,920
Well, this is a bit strange, isn't it?

649
01:03:56,000 --> 01:04:00,840
You're not usually
into history or archaeology.

650
01:04:00,920 --> 01:04:04,960
You were born in Ayutthaya, yet you've
barely visited any of the sites.

651
01:04:06,600 --> 01:04:08,560
You seem especially happy today,
don't you?

652
01:04:10,320 --> 01:04:12,320
Your senior's here to take you out, huh?

653
01:04:17,800 --> 01:04:18,880
Phop.

654
01:04:19,680 --> 01:04:22,840
I must thank you,

655
01:04:23,680 --> 01:04:26,160
and please take care of Nakun for me.

656
01:04:30,560 --> 01:04:32,440
Of course, Mother.

657
01:04:38,360 --> 01:04:40,120
The bathroom…

658
01:04:41,400 --> 01:04:43,880
It's to the left of the entrance.

659
01:04:43,960 --> 01:04:44,880
Thank you.

660
01:04:56,640 --> 01:05:00,160
Now, there is no need to be so tense.

661
01:05:01,160 --> 01:05:03,960
Whether he's your friend, your senior,

662
01:05:04,040 --> 01:05:06,600
or your boyfriend,

663
01:05:06,680 --> 01:05:08,240
I've got no problem with it.

664
01:05:08,320 --> 01:05:12,320
I'm really happy for you.

665
01:05:14,640 --> 01:05:15,520
It's not that, Mom.

666
01:05:16,560 --> 01:05:18,240
There's something else on my mind.

667
01:05:25,160 --> 01:05:27,080
Phop

668
01:05:28,440 --> 01:05:30,880
took me on a trip today…

669
01:05:33,360 --> 01:05:34,360
and

670
01:05:36,240 --> 01:05:38,880
I heard a story

671
01:05:39,400 --> 01:05:41,480
about a certain Ayutthaya-era high lord.

672
01:05:44,240 --> 01:05:45,560
Mom, do you know

673
01:05:46,400 --> 01:05:48,400
who Lord Preechaphibal was?

674
01:05:58,160 --> 01:05:59,240
I don't.

675
01:06:02,760 --> 01:06:03,680
But

676
01:06:03,760 --> 01:06:07,200
my old surname used to include "Preecha."

677
01:06:07,960 --> 01:06:09,600
"Satjapreecha."

678
01:06:09,680 --> 01:06:14,160
It means "knowledge rooted in integrity."

679
01:06:15,160 --> 01:06:19,480
Our family really stands by this meaning,

680
01:06:19,560 --> 01:06:21,800
as we are officials.

681
01:06:21,880 --> 01:06:24,040
In our family's eyes,

682
01:06:24,120 --> 01:06:27,920
working as an official
is the same as holding real power.

683
01:06:28,000 --> 01:06:28,920
That means

684
01:06:29,000 --> 01:06:32,800
we must work with dedication and honesty,

685
01:06:32,880 --> 01:06:36,160
and most importantly, never take bribes.

686
01:06:39,400 --> 01:06:40,240
Hey.

687
01:06:41,000 --> 01:06:42,560
Don't tell me

688
01:06:42,640 --> 01:06:43,960
you think

689
01:06:44,040 --> 01:06:46,920
this lord guy
was the forefather of our family.

690
01:06:49,760 --> 01:06:51,960
I think it might be you…

691
01:06:54,480 --> 01:06:55,560
I'm sorry?

692
01:07:05,480 --> 01:07:07,200
You and he are identical.

693
01:07:08,440 --> 01:07:10,440
There is no doubt
you're his reincarnation.

694
01:07:18,880 --> 01:07:20,040
Forget I said that, Mom.

695
01:07:20,840 --> 01:07:23,400
My mind was all over the place.

696
01:07:28,400 --> 01:07:29,240
Nakun.

697
01:07:33,280 --> 01:07:34,440
Are you sick?

698
01:07:37,320 --> 01:07:38,200
I think

699
01:07:38,920 --> 01:07:40,040
you're burning up.

700
01:07:40,120 --> 01:07:41,280
I think you…

701
01:07:47,040 --> 01:07:47,880
Mom.

702
01:07:49,760 --> 01:07:50,760
I'm…

703
01:07:52,760 --> 01:07:54,240
I'm so grateful…

704
01:07:56,320 --> 01:07:57,160
to

705
01:07:58,720 --> 01:08:00,720
have been born as your son in this life.

706
01:08:15,520 --> 01:08:17,000
What about your next one?

707
01:08:26,040 --> 01:08:28,399
I hope I can be your son
in every lifetime.

708
01:08:53,720 --> 01:08:55,000
I love you, sweetie.

709
01:08:57,640 --> 01:08:58,920
I love you too, Mom.

710
01:09:29,279 --> 01:09:31,560
Your mother's house is close to my manor.

711
01:09:31,640 --> 01:09:34,880
That's why you were transported
from the mango orchard to there.

712
01:09:35,520 --> 01:09:38,760
That's why everything and everyone
eventually came back together.

713
01:09:42,840 --> 01:09:44,439
As for those we don't meet here,

714
01:09:45,760 --> 01:09:48,479
they may have reincarnated
in a different gender

715
01:09:49,040 --> 01:09:50,640
or appearance,

716
01:09:50,720 --> 01:09:51,840
like my mom.

717
01:09:52,880 --> 01:09:54,320
Though appearances may change,

718
01:09:55,200 --> 01:09:58,240
the mind journeys on.

719
01:10:02,000 --> 01:10:05,080
My professor
in my time-travel literature class said

720
01:10:05,160 --> 01:10:07,640
that sometimes,
when it comes to time travel,

721
01:10:08,160 --> 01:10:10,680
we cannot simply rely on logic,

722
01:10:10,760 --> 01:10:12,280
but instead on emotions,

723
01:10:12,360 --> 01:10:14,800
hope, and fear.

724
01:10:15,800 --> 01:10:17,160
She once asked me,

725
01:10:17,760 --> 01:10:19,560
"You have no fear?"

726
01:10:20,840 --> 01:10:22,640
But now I realize that…

727
01:10:26,240 --> 01:10:28,200
after my parents separated,

728
01:10:29,840 --> 01:10:31,960
what I fear is change,

729
01:10:32,920 --> 01:10:34,440
separation,

730
01:10:35,040 --> 01:10:36,680
and love itself,

731
01:10:37,680 --> 01:10:39,960
because I don't want to lose that person.

732
01:10:43,080 --> 01:10:45,840
But after time traveling
and meeting you…

733
01:10:48,040 --> 01:10:49,520
what I've come to realize is that

734
01:10:50,400 --> 01:10:52,240
I shouldn't fixate on the past

735
01:10:53,120 --> 01:10:54,320
or be afraid of the future

736
01:10:56,040 --> 01:10:57,280
because right now,

737
01:10:58,200 --> 01:10:59,080
right here,

738
01:10:59,880 --> 01:11:00,920
at this very moment…

739
01:11:04,760 --> 01:11:06,040
the present

740
01:11:07,360 --> 01:11:08,840
is the most valuable to me.

741
01:11:20,720 --> 01:11:22,160
If that's the case,

742
01:11:22,240 --> 01:11:23,840
let's make the most of the present.

743
01:11:27,960 --> 01:11:29,120
Let's take a shower first,

744
01:11:30,440 --> 01:11:32,160
then we can hold each other and sleep.

745
01:11:40,160 --> 01:11:41,320
Well then,

746
01:11:41,400 --> 01:11:44,040
kindly have the water heated for me.

747
01:11:44,640 --> 01:11:46,360
I dislike bathing in the canal.

748
01:11:46,960 --> 01:11:48,160
It cannot be done,

749
01:11:48,880 --> 01:11:50,200
for there is no canal here.

750
01:11:52,920 --> 01:11:56,400
A whirlpool bathtub
and a water heater await you.

751
01:12:00,400 --> 01:12:01,240
Hey!

752
01:12:05,120 --> 01:12:06,720
Hey, Phop.

753
01:12:24,080 --> 01:12:25,080
It smells so good.

754
01:12:27,120 --> 01:12:28,640
Can we use it every night?

755
01:12:30,160 --> 01:12:32,440
I want to kiss
your head like this every night.

756
01:12:33,760 --> 01:12:35,040
Phop.

757
01:12:36,320 --> 01:12:38,120
Wait until my hair is dry first.

758
01:12:39,720 --> 01:12:41,520
Haven't I waited long enough?

759
01:17:10,400 --> 01:17:12,000
This feels like a dream, doesn't it?

760
01:17:12,560 --> 01:17:14,960
Who'd have thought we'd find
our way back to each other?

761
01:17:15,880 --> 01:17:18,880
It's probably because of
the fortune teller's wishing stone.

762
01:17:20,360 --> 01:17:22,560
Back at the hut by the pond,

763
01:17:23,840 --> 01:17:25,840
when you told me that

764
01:17:25,920 --> 01:17:28,800
Cherd had his men threw
Pim and Kla's bodies into the pond,

765
01:17:29,440 --> 01:17:31,600
I had my patrolmen search for them.

766
01:17:40,080 --> 01:17:42,080
<i>One of my men found something.</i>

767
01:18:10,320 --> 01:18:13,520
<i>The next day,</i>
<i>I went to ask Jom and Kaew about it.</i>

768
01:18:16,920 --> 01:18:18,680
<i>I found out that</i>

769
01:18:19,200 --> 01:18:21,880
<i>the oracle also gave Kaew another stone.</i>

770
01:18:39,320 --> 01:18:40,800
<i>I never understood this.</i>

771
01:18:41,680 --> 01:18:44,240
<i>Klao disappeared when Cherd shot me,</i>

772
01:18:44,840 --> 01:18:47,480
<i>but why was his body</i>
<i>at the bottom of the pond?</i>

773
01:19:02,400 --> 01:19:06,840
<i>Despite that, I kept the stone</i>
<i>until I drew my final breath.</i>

774
01:19:13,240 --> 01:19:17,280
<i>I made a wish</i>
<i>to be reincarnated somewhere close to you,</i>

775
01:19:18,560 --> 01:19:20,320
<i>to remember who you were,</i>

776
01:19:21,160 --> 01:19:22,920
<i>and to have a chance</i>
<i>to love you once more.</i>

777
01:19:24,280 --> 01:19:26,480
<i>Then I will love you as much as I can.</i>

778
01:19:31,720 --> 01:19:33,840
<i>After that, the light in me simply faded</i>

779
01:19:34,600 --> 01:19:35,840
<i>as I lay there alone.</i>

780
01:19:44,720 --> 01:19:47,120
Maybe it wasn't the stone at all,

781
01:19:48,360 --> 01:19:50,720
but rather how much I love

782
01:19:50,800 --> 01:19:52,400
and long for you.

783
01:19:53,600 --> 01:19:55,360
That's why we found each other again.

784
01:20:03,800 --> 01:20:05,520
Well, I'm right here.

785
01:20:07,360 --> 01:20:09,000
I won't keep you waiting anymore.

786
01:20:10,160 --> 01:20:12,000
I won't slip out of your arms either.

787
01:20:17,320 --> 01:20:19,200
If you do,
I will find my way to you again.

788
01:20:21,560 --> 01:20:23,440
Even if death tears us apart,

789
01:20:24,560 --> 01:20:27,040
I will find my way back to you
in every lifetime.

790
01:20:31,400 --> 01:20:32,240
And…

791
01:20:33,280 --> 01:20:35,640
What if we don't recognize each other
in the next life?

792
01:20:36,360 --> 01:20:40,080
Or what if the miracle
doesn't happen next time?

793
01:20:44,080 --> 01:20:45,320
It's not a problem at all.

794
01:20:46,000 --> 01:20:48,440
Let's love each other
as best as we can in this life.

795
01:21:01,080 --> 01:21:03,680
I've imagined this moment in many ways.

796
01:21:05,760 --> 01:21:07,160
How should I ask you?

797
01:21:07,960 --> 01:21:09,320
When would be the right time?

798
01:21:10,520 --> 01:21:11,960
Where would be the perfect place?

799
01:21:13,960 --> 01:21:15,480
But in the end,

800
01:21:16,400 --> 01:21:17,960
I just know this is the moment.

801
01:21:21,840 --> 01:21:23,080
I can't wait any longer.

802
01:21:39,840 --> 01:21:42,720
My mom told me this is a family heirloom.

803
01:21:48,840 --> 01:21:50,840
You'll probably graduate in 2025…

804
01:21:53,280 --> 01:21:55,720
just as the Marriage Equality Act
is likely to pass.

805
01:22:01,680 --> 01:22:03,280
When that time comes…

806
01:22:05,720 --> 01:22:07,040
will you

807
01:22:08,000 --> 01:22:08,880
marry me?

808
01:22:14,480 --> 01:22:15,720
Yes.

809
01:22:16,840 --> 01:22:17,680
Certainly,

810
01:22:18,600 --> 01:22:19,680
my Lord.

811
01:22:36,960 --> 01:22:38,600
We met here,

812
01:22:38,680 --> 01:22:40,520
so we want to register our marriage

813
01:22:40,600 --> 01:22:42,360
and get married right here.

814
01:22:43,240 --> 01:22:44,080
Yes.

815
01:22:44,160 --> 01:22:47,360
I wanted to register our marriage
when the Marriage Equality Act passed,

816
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:50,560
but the date the oracle gave us… Sorry.

817
01:22:50,640 --> 01:22:52,000
I mean, the fortune teller…

818
01:22:52,080 --> 01:22:55,320
It was a different date,
so we chose to register today.

819
01:22:55,400 --> 01:22:58,080
We will then show a special video
for everyone in attendance.

820
01:23:09,080 --> 01:23:10,840
Since meeting Nakun,

821
01:23:10,920 --> 01:23:13,160
Phop has become more talkative and lively.

822
01:23:13,840 --> 01:23:16,880
He hasn't been as sad
and lonely as he used to be.

823
01:23:17,560 --> 01:23:20,680
I guess that's what he gets
from being with Nakun.

824
01:23:20,760 --> 01:23:24,000
When we become one family,

825
01:23:24,080 --> 01:23:26,320
I'm afraid they might end up
talking over each other

826
01:23:26,400 --> 01:23:28,720
and not listening to one another.

827
01:23:28,800 --> 01:23:29,640
I agree.

828
01:23:32,520 --> 01:23:34,560
Cut. Thank you so much.

829
01:23:40,720 --> 01:23:41,760
Hello.

830
01:23:51,600 --> 01:23:55,720
Congratulations. The Marriage Equality Act
is finally official.

831
01:23:57,040 --> 01:23:58,800
I wish you both a beautiful love story.

832
01:24:00,440 --> 01:24:03,520
May I ask who will be signing
as the witness?

833
01:24:08,920 --> 01:24:10,600
Please sign here.

834
01:24:14,560 --> 01:24:15,760
Congratulations, Nakun.

835
01:24:37,040 --> 01:24:38,560
Why are you crying, Thee?

836
01:24:39,720 --> 01:24:41,120
I'm feeling emotional.

837
01:24:41,200 --> 01:24:42,960
Nakun is finally off the market.

838
01:24:44,640 --> 01:24:48,000
Please sign here,
both spouses.

839
01:24:48,080 --> 01:24:49,200
One moment.

840
01:25:20,080 --> 01:25:22,480
Let me take care of you
until the end of time…

841
01:25:24,520 --> 01:25:26,240
my spouse.

842
01:25:41,320 --> 01:25:43,560
I will also take the best care of you,

843
01:25:44,360 --> 01:25:46,360
to make the wait worth it.

844
01:25:50,840 --> 01:25:53,320
You both have been waiting
a long time for this day.

845
01:25:53,400 --> 01:25:54,240
Yes.

846
01:25:55,200 --> 01:25:56,640
For 400 years.

847
01:26:05,240 --> 01:26:07,360
Please sign right here.

848
01:26:27,800 --> 01:26:32,120
I now pronounce you
legally married spouses.

849
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:43,600
<i>And have you not considered it?</i>

850
01:26:43,680 --> 01:26:45,040
<i>How would you and Phop</i>

851
01:26:45,120 --> 01:26:46,440
<i>live together</i>

852
01:26:46,520 --> 01:26:48,520
without inviting cruel gossip?

853
01:26:48,600 --> 01:26:50,640
<i>No good</i>

854
01:26:50,720 --> 01:26:52,840
can come from two men being together.

855
01:26:52,920 --> 01:26:54,320
At least

856
01:26:54,400 --> 01:26:56,440
for the time being.

857
01:26:57,200 --> 01:26:59,240
<i>If there is a next life,</i>

858
01:26:59,320 --> 01:27:01,160
<i>I hope we'll meet again</i>

859
01:27:01,920 --> 01:27:03,840
<i>in a world where men</i>
<i>can fall in love freely.</i>

860
01:27:06,400 --> 01:27:09,400
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE

861
01:27:24,880 --> 01:27:29,680
TO A LOVE UNBOUND BY GENDER
DEFYING THE TIDES OF TIME
